OL,3,GNEWSABoy nearly crushed by tree downed
OL,4,Aby lightning
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman has described the terrifying
OL,7,Fmoment when lightning struck a huge
OL,8,Ftree next to her home and nearly
OL,9,Fcrushed her five-year-old son.
OL,11,FKatelyn Moore, from Rugby, said she had
OL,12,Fpulled up after a shopping trip last
OL,13,Fweek and her son ran towards their home
OL,14,Fjust as lightning hit the tree making
OL,15,Fan "enormous bang", sounding "like a
OL,16,Fgunshot".
OL,18,FShe said the tree suddenly came
OL,19,Fcrashing down, with the leaves covering
OL,20,Fher son, before he emerged unscathed
OL,21,Ffrom beneath some branches.
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,355,350,200,160,0,100
